---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Career history and background of Alejandro Ojeda-Celis.">
  <section class="page-head section profile-header">
    <div class="profile-avatar-container">
      <img 
        src="/me.jpg" 
        alt="Alejandro Ojeda-Celis" 
        class="profile-avatar"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="profile-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">About & Career History</p>
      <h1>Alejandro Ojeda-Celis</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Computer Science graduate and software engineer based in Arlington, TX. Bilingual in English and Spanish, specializing in data engineering, PostgreSQL database architecture, and operational process optimization.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Career Timeline / Narrative -->
  <section class="section prose-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Career History</p>
      <h2>Education to Production</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        My technical foundation began at the <strong>University of Texas at Arlington</strong>, where I earned my <strong>Bachelor of Science in Computer Science</strong> (GPA: 3.28/4.0) in August 2024. Through coursework in <em>Algorithms & Data Structures</em>, <em>Database Systems & File Structures</em>, and <em>Artificial Intelligence</em>, I developed a strong core in system design, relational data management, and algorithmic thinking.
      </p>

      <p>
        In September 2025, I joined <strong>Hub Financial</strong> as a Commercial Tracking Analyst in Irving, TX. In this role, I designed an Excel tracking architecture to log and analyze document processing speeds, establishing the department's baseline key performance indicators (KPIs). Additionally, I authored detailed technical feedback summaries for the Learning & Development (L&D) team to fix documentation gaps and streamline the onboarding pipeline for new hires.
      </p>

      <p>
        Parallel to my enterprise work, I served as a Sports Data Analyst Volunteer for <strong>Next Play Nation Basketball</strong> from October 2025 through January 2026. Working hands-on with operational data, I wrote custom LibreOffice Basic macros to improve score maintenance accuracy by over 40% and built custom spreadsheet formulas that enhanced overall data precision by 24%.
      </p>

      <p>
        In April 2026, I transitioned to <strong>Insight</strong> in Fort Worth, TX as a Service Technician. Here, I developed custom Excel scripts to filter, manage, and track real-time completion states for high-volume daily order queues—boosting team throughput. I also led quality control initiatives by updating critical technical documentation, cutting client-side operational errors by over 50%.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Experience & Education Ledger -->
  <section class="section" aria-label="Experience ledger">
    <p class="eyebrow">Timeline Breakdown</p>
    <div class="about-ledger">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Insight — Service Technician</h3>
        <p><strong>April 2026 – Present | Fort Worth, TX</strong></p>
        <p>Engineered daily order tracking scripts and revamped critical documentation to reduce operational error rates by 50%.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Hub Financial — Commercial Tracking Analyst</h3>
        <p><strong>Sept 2025 – April 2026 | Irving, TX</strong></p>
        <p>Architected document processing KPI tracking systems and published L&D feedback summaries to streamline team onboarding.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Next Play Nation — Sports Data Analyst (Volunteer)</h3>
        <p><strong>Oct 2025 – Jan 2026 | Arlington, TX</strong></p>
        <p>Automated score accuracy (+40%) and data validation (+24%) using LibreOffice Basic macros and custom functions.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>04</span>
        <h3>UT Arlington — B.S. in Computer Science</h3>
        <p><strong>Graduated August 2024 | Arlington, TX</strong></p>
        <p>GPA: 3.28/4.0. Core focus in algorithms, relational database structures, AI, and software engineering principles.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Technical Stack Summary -->
  <section class="section prose-grid about-closing">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Technical Capabilities</p>
      <h2>Tools & Ecosystems</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        <strong>Languages & Core:</strong> Python, SQL/SQLite, PostgreSQL (Supabase), TypeScript, HTML/CSS, JSON Processing.<br />
        <strong>Cloud & Data Engineering:</strong> Google Cloud Platform (BigQuery, Cloud Storage), Automated Cron Jobs, REST APIs.<br />
        <strong>Analytics & Tools:</strong> Tableau, Power BI, Microsoft Excel (Advanced Scripting/Macros), Git, Linux, SAP.<br />
        <strong>Languages Spoken:</strong> English (Fluent), Spanish (Fluent).
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .profile-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .profile-header {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 3rem;
    }
  }

  .profile-avatar-container {
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .profile-avatar {
    width: 200px;
    height: 200px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 2px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
    background-color: #1a1a1a;
  }

  .profile-intro {
    flex: 1;
  }

  .about-ledger article p strong {
    color: var(--color-text, #fff);
  }
</style>